  "body": "The three findings of the Claude release review of `threepipe@0.7.0-next.0`, `@threepipe/plugin-annotations@0.1.0-next.0` and `@threepipe/plugin-cloud@0.1.0-next.0` that need a change on `dev`. Each was checked against the code before fixing.\n\n**plugin-cloud: a page without storage asks before it takes a key** (`plugins/cloud/src/auth/CloudAuth.ts`)\n- `signIn()` keeps a random `state` in sessionStorage, and `handleRedirect()` only takes a key that brings it back. A sandboxed page (files.threepipe.org, CSP `sandbox` without `allow-same-origin`) has no storage, so it skipped the check and took any key in the URL. A link carrying someone else's key (`#tp_cloud_key=…`) signed the visitor in to that account, and their saves, shares and reports went there.\n- Such a page now asks first: \"Sign in to threepipe cloud as <account>?\". `<account>` is the email the key was issued to (`sub`, from services/cloud `mintKey`), read from the key itself. `tp_cloud_user` is plain text in the link, so the dialog doesn't use it. Changing the claim would break the key's signature.\n- `auth.confirmUnverified(account) => boolean` replaces the `confirm()` dialog with the app's own. Where `confirm()` isn't available (a sandbox without `allow-modals`), there is no sign-in. Pages with storage check the `state` as before and never ask. A key from another endpoint is refused before anything is asked.\n- Cost: on files.threepipe.org, apps sign in on every load, so that's one extra click per load there. The review's suggestion of carrying the state in the return URL doesn't help, because whoever makes the link controls the whole URL.\n\n**CHANGELOG:** an Added entry for `CanvasRecorderPlugin.frameSink` (`DirectoryFrameSink`, `ZipFrameSink`), `registerRecorder` and `unregisterRecorder`. #184 added them without one.\n\n**plugin-cloud CHANGELOG:** the `## 0.1.0` section described a version that was never published, so the stable release would have passed the changelog check without notes for the fixes since. `[Unreleased]` now holds the whole first version: Added, Security, Fixed. `website/package/plugin-cloud.md` describes the dialog.\n\n**Checked**\n- `npm test` in plugins/cloud: 17 tests pass. Five new ones cover the dialog on a page without storage: it names the key's account and not `tp_cloud_user`, OK signs in, Cancel, a missing or throwing `confirm()` and a key with no account all leave the page signed out, a custom `confirmUnverified` replaces the dialog, a page with storage never asks, and a key from another endpoint is refused without asking. `npm run typecheck` in plugins/cloud passes.\n- In Chromium, with the built plugin on a page served with the CSP of files.threepipe.org (`sandbox allow-scripts allow-forms allow-popups allow-modals …`) and a key for `attacker@example.com` with `tp_cloud_user=palash` in the URL:\n  - sessionStorage throws `SecurityError`\n  - the dialog says \"Sign in to threepipe cloud as attacker@example.com?\"\n  - Cancel → `handleRedirect()` returns `null` and the page stays signed out; OK → `'signed-in'`\n  - the key is removed from the address bar either way\n- `npm run lint` and `npm run test:unit` (1102 tests) pass.\n\nNot in this PR:\n- republishing plugin-cloud: `0.1.0-next.0` (with the issue) stays npm's `latest` until the stable `0.1.0`, as decided\n- `next` keeps its `0.1.0-next.0` changelog section; the next merge of `dev` into `next` updates its wording\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01EWN5WJVoif5u2R5D96ps9b)_",
